    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="0597" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg479"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.404/1012</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of Mexican Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-06-22">June 22, 1929</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: Mr. Morrow telephoned at 5:15
                    yesterday evening to the effect that the religious situation had been settled,
                    and that the statements of President Portes Gil and Archbishop Ruiz<anchor
                        n="59" xml:id="d564-f1"/> had been or were about to be given to the press
                    for publication in the newspapers of June 22nd. Mr. Morrow asked me to
                    communicate the foregoing to yourself, Father Burke<anchor n="60"
                        xml:id="d564-f2"/> and Mr. Montavon.<anchor n="61" xml:id="d564-f3"/> I <pb
                        facs="0598" n="480" xml:id="pg480"/> was unable to reach you at your hotel
                    by telephone, but I was able to get in touch with Mr. Schoenfeld, who I
                    understand succeeded in conveying Mr. Morrow’s message to you.</p>
                <p>I informed Mr. Morrow of the proposed statement to be given out by the President
                    in case he were asked for comment on the settlement. Mr. Morrow said that he
                    thought it would have a very good effect and would be highly appreciated in
                    Mexico.</p>
                <closer><signed>A[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rthur</hi>] B[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">liss</hi>] L[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ane</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d564-f1" n="59" xml:id="d564-f1-content">
                <p>Leopoldo Ruiz, the senior prelate of the Mexican Church.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d564-f2" n="60" xml:id="d564-f2-content">
                <p>John J. Burke, General Secretary of the National Catholic Welfare Conference.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d564-f3" n="61" xml:id="d564-f3-content">
                <p>William F. Montavon, Legal Adviser of the National Catholic Welfare
                    Conference.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
